<!--
  Auld Lang Syne
  Traditional Scottish tune, words by Robert Burns (1788). Public domain.
  F major (the B flat is never played: the tune is pentatonic), 4/4, quarter = 80,
  pickup + 16 bars (48 s): verse and chorus. Melody only, C4-D5 (15 keys), in the C4-B5 window.

  bar | right hand  | words
    0 | C4          | Should
    1 | F4 F4 F4 A4 | auld ac-quain-tance
    2 | G4 F4 G4 A4 | be for-got, and
    3 | F4 F4 A4 C5 | nev-er brought to
    4 | D5 D5       | mind? Should
    5 | C5 A4 A4 F4 | auld ac-quain-tance
    6 | G4 F4 G4 A4 | be for-got, and
    7 | F4 D4 D4 C4 | auld lang
    8 | F4 D5       | syne? For
    9 | C5 A4 A4 F4 | auld lang
   10 | G4 F4 G4 D5 | syne, my dear, for
   11 | C5 A4 A4 C5 | auld lang
   12 | D5 D5       | syne, we'll
   13 | C5 A4 A4 F4 | tak' a cup o'
   14 | G4 F4 G4 A4 | kind-ness yet, for
   15 | F4 D4 D4 C4 | auld lang
   16 | F4          | syne.
-->
